WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.526
In a school, every pupil has a name, so you can call the right person. In a program, every variable, constant, array and subprogram has a name too. That name is called an identifier.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:28.504
Think of a recipe that says, add the fruit. Fruit is a placeholder. When you cook, you pass in real apples. In code, the placeholder in the def line is the parameter. The value passed in the call is the argument.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:44.700
Where a variable is made decides its scope. One made inside a def block is local. One made in the main program is global. And its first value shows its data type: zero point zero or float gives a real.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:01:03.209
First, underline exactly what kind of item is asked for. Then go to the right place. Def headers hold parameters. Call brackets hold arguments. The name left of equals a function call receives the returned value.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:12.101
Finally, copy the identifier exactly as it is spelt, with the same capitals. Do not give a line number when a name is asked for.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:23.842
Here is a real question from Paper 2 in June 2025. Identify the name of a parameter. It is worth one mark.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:34.316
Here is the program, rebuilt by olevels.com. Find the subprogram header. Def get wages, with in sales and in age in the brackets.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:45.294
The names inside the header brackets are the parameters: in sales and in age. Sales and age on the last line are different. They are the arguments passed in the call.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:57.276
So write one parameter, spelt exactly: in sales, with a capital S. Either parameter earns the mark. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:08.208
The most common mistake is mixing up parameters and arguments. Sales is passed in the call, so it is an argument, not a parameter.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:21.217
Another mistake is naming a global variable when a local one is asked for. Wages is made inside the def block, so it is local. Sales is made in the main program, so it is global.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:34.973
Now you try. From this code, identify a parameter, a local variable, the variable that receives the returned value, and a constant. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:50.109
A parameter is p length or p width, in the def line. Result is made inside the def block, so it is local. Answer receives the returned value on line six. Rate, in capitals, is the constant.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:59.957
Remember the method: know the kind of item, go to its place in the code, and copy the name exactly. Now try the practice questions for this type.
